  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "note_14",
      "text": "WORKFLOW: arrhythmic record (negative control). This is the most useful thing to look at BEFORE interpreting your own data. Two records with the same average activity are analysed identically: one intact, one arrhythmic (as after SCN ablation). Notice what does NOT happen: the arrhythmic periodogram does not go blank. A periodogram always returns its largest value, so it still reports a 'peak period', and read alone that number is meaningless. What separates the two is the POWER at that peak and the actogram, where the intact record shows an obvious band and the arrhythmic one shows nothing. If you take one habit from this library, take this: never report a peak period without its power and a look at the raw record.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 24,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 190
    }
